#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# right_composition

#% text
# `right_composition(f, g, ...)` is the function that applies the functions left to right: `right_composition(f, g)(x)` is `g(f(x))`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is `composition` with the functions in the opposite order.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
right_composition(f, g)(x)
#% output
#= g(f(x))

#% cell
right_composition(abs, sqrt)(-16)
#% output
#= 4

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The reverse order of `composition`:

#% cell
right_composition(f, g, h)(x) === composition(h, g, f)(x)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `composition`, `fold`
